	The bones file goes away when it's loaded into an active game.
He's encountered the level in his current game, so there is no more
bones file... it's been subsumed into the game-in-progress. If he dies
now, a new bones file may be created... but only of the level he dies
on. If he dies on the level with the titan, there's a chance (not 100%)
that it'll create a new bones file of that level. If he dies on some
other level, it won't create a new bones of the titan level, so the
titan bones will be gone.

